[Term]
id: EMPTY:0000224
name: subject text identifier
def: "A categorical identifier consisting of a string of alphanumeric characters assigned by an investigator to uniquely label a subject. Unlike numerical codes, these often include descriptive prefixes related to the study or cohort." []
is_a: EMPTY:0000084 ! categorical identifier

[Term]
id: EMPTY:0000225
name: subject enumerated identifier
def: "An enumerated identifier assigned to an experimental subject based on a sequential numbering system, used to distinguish individuals within a specific group or trial." []
is_a: EMPTY:0000083 ! enumerated identifier

[Term]
id: EMPTY:0000226
name: experiment metadata file
def: "A digital document containing structured data that describes the context, parameters, and environmental conditions under which an experiment was performed. It serves to ensure the reproducibility and interpretability of the primary experimental data." []

[Term]
id: EMPTY:0000227
name: data-independent acquisition (DIA)
def: "A method of molecular analysis, typically in mass spectrometry, where all ions within a specified m/z range are fragmented and analyzed together. This approach provides a comprehensive and reproducible digital record of the sample without the stochastic sampling bias found in data-dependent acquisition." []

[Term]
id: EMPTY:0000228
name: slide scanner image acquisition
def: "A process of generating high-resolution digital representations of whole histological sections mounted on glass slides using an automated microscopy system. This enables large-scale quantitative analysis of tissue morphology and marker expression." []

[Term]
id: EMPTY:0000229
name: echocardiogram acquisition
def: "A non-invasive procedure that uses ultrasound waves to generate real-time images of the heart's structure and function. In an experimental context, it is used to measure parameters such as chamber dimensions, wall thickness, and blood flow velocity." []

[Term]
id: EMPTY:0000230
name: unknown electronic file type
def: "A digital file for which the format, encoding, or origin cannot be definitively identified by the system or investigator, necessitating further manual review or specialized software for interpretation." []

